.TH WMSETTINGS 1 "wm-desktop" "wm-desktop" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wmsettings \- the few settings the wm-desktop tools share
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wmsettings
list | get \fIKEY\fR | set \fIKEY\fR \fIVALUE\fR | apply [\-\-dry\-run]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Settings are validated and stored in a small file ($WMCONFIG_FILE, else $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/wm-desktop/settings.conf, default ~/.config/wm-desktop/settings.conf). \fBlist\fR shows every key
with its value and allowed values; \fBapply\fR writes the ones that map to Window Maker defaults into the Window Maker
defaults file (backing it up first). Keys: focus, placement, icon_size, animations, dock, terminal, icon_theme,
notify_corner, notify_dnd, notify_mute, notify_app_timeout, notify_timeout.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wmnotify (1),
.BR wmnotifyctl (1)
